From 3fa57b3222f73ef34fd21b21212aaf5705cddc11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:05:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ColorFade: Destroy the EGL surface after detaching it

dismissResources() and destroy() destroyed the EGL surface while it
was still current. EGL then only marks the surface for deletion, but
libEGL disconnects its window as soon as eglDestroySurface() returns.
The Mali-400 driver still holds a dequeued buffer at that point and
cancels it only when the surface is released at eglMakeCurrent(), so
BufferQueue freed a buffer that was still dequeued
("clearBuffersForDisconnectLocked: 1 buffers were freed while being
dequeued!", "Surface::cancelBuffer given a leaked buffer!"). On older
releases this crashed system_server when the screen turned off.

Destroy the surface after the context is detached.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G5iyKS6HLKv7fpZZf1pvxH
Change-Id: I8399753b4ffe18e4bef59fa110b53d1e159ad685
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java   | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
index 49e18b75276e..fa0a0b9714d2 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
@@ -380,10 +380,14 @@ final class ColorFade {
                 destroyScreenshotTexture();
                 destroyGLShaders();
                 destroyGLBuffers();
-                destroyEglSurface();
             } finally {
                 detachEglContext();
             }
+            // Destroy the surface only once it is no longer current. A current
+            // surface is only marked for deletion, but libEGL disconnects its
+            // window right away, while the driver may still hold a dequeued
+            // buffer that it cancels when the surface is finally released.
+            destroyEglSurface();
             // This is being called with no active context so shouldn't be
             // needed but is safer to not change for now.
             GLES20.glFlush();
@@ -427,10 +431,10 @@ final class ColorFade {
                     destroyScreenshotTexture();
                     destroyGLShaders();
                     destroyGLBuffers();
-                    destroyEglSurface();
                 } finally {
                     detachEglContext();
                 }
+                destroyEglSurface();
             }
             destroyEglContext();
             destroySurface();
-- 
